  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 408 AM EST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nLatest radar mosaic early this morning has widespread showers across \nmuch of the U.P. as a low pressure system now rotates directly over \nthe U.P. As this parent low integrates into a descending trough from \nCanada through the course of the day, rain showers will become most \nconcentrated over northern portions of the U.P. where an additional \n0.25\" of accumulation is possible. Following this wave will be, yet, \nanother secondary shortwave in the upper flow that will help \nreinforce CAA into the region through early tomorrow. This surge of \ncold air will transition the lake enhanced rain to lake effect snow \nstarting across the western portions of the U.P. late this \nafternoon/evening where temperatures will be in the low to mid 30s. \nAnticipate a rain/snow mix period through the evening hours before \nthat transition to pure lake effect snow after Fri 06Z. Across the \neast, it will be tougher for that rain to snow transition, where \ndaytime surface temperatures will run almost 10 degrees higher than \nthe western half. Therefore, it is very possible that the eastern \ncounties only reach a rain/snow mix by tomorrow morning, whereas the \nMichigamme Highlands could see their first measurable snowfall of \nthe season in the 1-2 inch range. While thermodynamic profiles show \nample low level moisture, lake inversions will have a tough time \nreaching the DGZ, thus preventing any big snowfall totals. Also \naccompanying the CAA and precipitation will be strong NNE winds \nlater this morning with widespread 35 to 45 mph winds across the \nnorthern Keweenaw and shorelines of Lake Superior. Look for these to \neventually taper off from west to east tomorrow morning.   \n\nFurther out, drier weather will return for the weekend as high \npressure strengthens over the area, and once again there will be a \nslight warmup into the 50s from Sunday through Tuesday. This will be \nafter a brief dip in high temperatures into the upper 30s/low 40s \ntomorrow and widespread 40s on Saturday. Meanwhile, though, \novernight lows will dip into the 20s through the extended period \n(and even as low as the teens across the interior west tomorrow \nnight).",
